## Introduction

This chart bootstraps a [Logging operator](https://github.com/kube-logging/logging-operator) deployment on a [Kubernetes](http://kubernetes.io) cluster using the [Helm](https://helm.sh) package manager.

## Prerequisites

- Kubernetes 1.19+

## Installing CRDs

Use `createCustomResource=false` with Helm v3 to avoid trying to create CRDs from the `crds` folder and from templates at the same time.

{{ template "chart.valuesSection" . }}

## Installing Fluentd and Fluent-bit via logging

The chart does **not** install `logging` resource to deploy Fluentd (or Syslog-ng) and Fluent-bit on the cluster by default, but
it can be enabled by setting the `logging.enabled` value to true.

### Multiline exceptions and Fluentd workers

See [values-multiline-example.yaml](values-multiline-example.yaml) for CRI fragment
reassembly followed by Java and Python exception detection in Fluent Bit, and two
Fluentd workers. The multiline filter is optional and runs before the other
filters. Use `customParsers` for additional multiline parser definitions.
The example assumes CRI container logs; adapt the tail parser for other runtimes.
Remove Fluentd `detectExceptions` filters when moving exception detection to
Fluent Bit, and ensure all remaining Fluentd plugins support multiple workers.
Buffered multiline records are held in memory by default; configure emitter
storage and limits for your deployment if needed.
